{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe reconciler active-set query hardcoded status != \"Done\" as the only Done-equivalent\n(fetcher.py jql_active / jql_done_recent). Against a live CLIENT Jira whose workflow uses\nClosed / Resolved / Cancelled (common), issues in those statuses are NOT \"Done\", so:\n- jql_active pulled Closed/Resolved issues into the active working set -> the reconciler\n  treated resolved issues as active and could push outbound mutations at them.\n- jql_done_recent missed them, so they never populated the recent-Done snapshot.\nThis mis-scoped the entire active set for any non-DIG/REB workflow.\n\n## Approach\nSwitch the Done predicate from the literal status = \"Done\" to Jira's status CATEGORY:\nstatusCategory = Done / statusCategory != Done, which is workflow-agnostic (every Jira\nstatus maps to one of To Do / In Progress / Done categories, including custom Closed/\nResolved/Cancelled statuses which map to the Done category). Keep the JQL builders'\nper-project scoping and _validate_project_key unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. jql_active excludes any status in the Done statusCategory (not just literal \"Done\").\n2. jql_done_recent selects the Done statusCategory, ORDER BY updated DESC, cap preserved.\n3. Single-project + multi-project fan-out unchanged otherwise; DIG/REB (To Do/In\n   Progress/Done only) behavior is identical.\n\n## Test plan\n- Update/extend the JQL-builder unit tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py\n  (and the fetch/ + orchestrate/ jql-string tests) to assert the statusCategory predicate.\n- RED first: a test encoding a client workflow with a \"Resolved\" status shows the OLD\n  status != \"Done\" query would include Resolved in active (bug), and the NEW query excludes it.\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits fetcher.py jql builders AND tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py,\nwhich ticket A also edits — this ticket is SEQUENCED AFTER ticket A (a01d) to avoid a\nfile conflict. Rebased onto A's landed change before starting."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786822181779021001,"uuid":"f66cc386-4cc8-491b-933c-acf74f3ec849"}